---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { codeTheme, standaloneCode } from '../../content/examples';
import Documentation from '../../layouts/Documentation.astro';
---
<Documentation>
  <p>Start with the <a href="/docs/installation">preview app</a>. In <code>main.ts</code>, find your target and its positioned host after mount:</p>
  <div class="docs-code-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Find the target and host"><Code code={`const host = document.querySelector('#host');
const target = document.querySelector('#target');
if (!(host instanceof HTMLElement) || !target) {
  throw new Error('Missing host or target');
}`} lang="ts" theme={codeTheme} /></div>
  <h2 id="attach-fire">Attach Fire</h2>
  <p>Add the following code to the same module. The ambient clock advances automatically. Fonts are ready before capture, and teardown is registered before initialization settles.</p>
  <div class="docs-code-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Standalone ambient attachment example"><Code code={standaloneCode} lang="ts" theme={codeTheme} /></div>
  <p>On component unmount, call <code>fire.dispose()</code> and remove your own listeners. The pagehide handler covers leaving the page; it does not replace framework teardown.</p>
  <h2 id="control-time">Control time and intensity</h2>
  <p><code>fire.pause()</code> freezes the ambient clock. <code>fire.resume()</code> continues without catching up time spent paused or hidden. Set <code>fire.intensity</code> to a finite value between 0 and 1; out-of-range finite values clamp.</p>
  <p>For explicit seeking, choose <code>clock: 'manual'</code> at creation and write <code>fire.time</code> in absolute seconds. Forward and backward seeks reuse the capture. A manual clock stays paused; <code>resume()</code> does not advance it.</p>
  <h2 id="refresh-and-cleanup">Refresh and cleanup</h2>
  <p>After changing captured paint, await <code>fire.refresh()</code>. It hides stale output and resolves once this or a newer revision commits. Observed target mutations and resize can refresh automatically; unobserved stylesheet, hover or ancestor paint changes still need explicit refresh.</p>
  <p>Disposal is idempotent and safe before <code>ready</code>. Removing an observed target or host is terminal; create a new attachment after remounting.</p>
  <h2 id="unavailable-output">Unavailable output</h2>
  <p><code>ready</code> resolves after an attempt, including environmental unavailability. Inspect <code>fire.lifecycle</code>, <code>fire.raster</code> and <code>fire.reason</code>. Keep the original content available. After correcting the condition, explicitly await <code>fire.retry()</code> and inspect the result again.</p>
  <p>The default <code>motion: 'respect'</code> suppresses output under reduced motion. Changing the preference back requires an explicit retry. <code>motion: 'static'</code> opts into a still decoration at time zero; it never overrides reduced motion with animation.</p>
  <p>See <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">troubleshooting</a> for typed reasons and recovery.</p>
</Documentation>
